{title: Pure in Heart}
{subtitle: Matthew 5:8}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 86}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | ×8

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Blessed are the meek, they inherit the earth
Hunger for right[Eb]eousness, their hearts are worth
Mercy flows [Cm]to those who show it first
Pure in [Gm]heart, seeing the divine burst
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Blessed are the pure in heart
For they will see [Eb]God apart
Blessed are [Cm]the pure in heart
For they will see [Gm]God apart
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Peacemakers called sons of the divine
[Eb]Persecuted for us, the kingdom is thine
[Cm]Insults and lies, spoken against your name
Re[Gm]joice in this truth, free from shame
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Blessed are the pure in heart
For they will see [Eb]God apart
Blessed are the [Cm]pure in heart
For they will see [Gm]God apart
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Gm] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] | [Cm] | [Cm] | [Gm] |
| [Gm] |

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
The earth is theirs, the fill is given
[Eb]Mercy received, the merciful are living
[Cm]Pure in heart, the vision is clear
[Gm]God is seen, drawing near
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Blessed are the pure in heart
For they will see [Eb]God apart
{end_of_verse}

